The EPUB reader menu's icon tab-bar layout (see
src/activities/reader/EpubReaderMenuActivity.h/.cpp: drawIconTabBar/tabSlotRect) is adapted from
CrossInk (https://github.com/uxjulia/CrossInk), also a fork of CrossPoint, licensed under the MIT
License. Navigation is CrossFade's own existing tab+list button scheme (see SettingsActivity).

The Lyra Carousel home theme (src/components/themes/lyra/LyraCarouselTheme.h/.cpp) is a functional
port of CrossInk's Lyra Carousel theme (https://github.com/uxjulia/CrossInk), also a fork of
CrossPoint, licensed under the MIT License, including its two-tier cover sizing, bidirectional
(both-axis) cover cropping, and title/dot/progress-bar layout, solved against this fork's own
screen dimensions rather than CrossInk's literal pixel constants. Adapted rather than copied
wholesale -- see that file's own header comment for what differs (no frame-cache pre-rendering, no
reading-stats text, CrossFade's own menu icon assets) and why.

GfxRenderer::drawPerspectiveBitmap (lib/GfxRenderer/GfxRenderer.h/.cpp), the trapezoid-warped
bitmap primitive behind Lyra Carousel's receding side covers, and the side-cover proportions that
use it, are ported from CrossInk's own GfxRenderer and LyraCarouselTheme
(https://github.com/uxjulia/CrossInk), also a fork of CrossPoint, licensed under the MIT License --
adapted to this fork's own row-buffer allocation pattern (malloc/free per call, matching this
file's existing drawBitmap, rather than CrossInk's pooled scratch allocator, which this fork
doesn't have); the per-column perspective math itself is unchanged.

The Reading Dashboard home theme (src/components/themes/dashboard/DashboardTheme.h/.cpp and
src/components/themes/dashboard/DashboardLayout.h) adapts the home-screen visual language of YACP's
Dashboard theme (https://github.com/Sichroteph/YACP, commit
a96da864647ddc23a28431582ad722a67ca689ba, src/components/themes/dashboard/DashboardTheme.cpp), also
a fork of CrossPoint, licensed under the MIT License: the single rounded primary reading card, the
inverted "Continue Reading" pill, the round icon tile, the rounded panel of caption-over-value stat
pairs, the full-width rounded action rows, and the rounded empty-state action pill. Adapted rather
than ported -- see that file's own header comment for what is deliberately left behind (YACP's
branding and logo, its reading-stats schema and the seven-row statistics column, its progress bar
and percentage, reader-type icons, sleep screen, and cover pipeline) and why. The layout arithmetic
is solved against this fork's own screen dimensions and measured font metrics, the card is sized to
its content rather than to a fixed frame, the book-selection semantics (pinned default, ephemeral
browse) are CrossFade's own, and the theme reuses CrossFade's existing home action builder, routes
and icon assets.

CrossFade modifications are likewise released under the MIT License.
